WEBVTT

asr-000067
00:31:28.720 --> 00:31:47.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: The consultation of the Committee on Finance, Subcommittee A, with civil society organizations to discuss budgetary priorities for the proposed fiscal year 2027 budget is hereby called to order. I'd like to acknowledge the presence of our colleague, Senator Panfilo Lacson.

asr-000068
00:31:48.800 --> 00:32:13.320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And before we recognize the resource persons, the Chair would like to state some guidelines for our orderly conduct for this afternoon. Due to the limited number of seats available at the panel, only one resource person per CSO will be seated at the panel. Should a question be addressed or answered by your colleague, you must first seek the permission of the Chair to have your colleague recognized before they may respond.

asr-000069
00:32:14.280 --> 00:32:48.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We would like also to remind everyone that each CSO is allotted a maximum of five minutes to deliver its statement or presentation. A timer will be displayed on the screen to help everyone keep track of their allotted time. Thank you for your understanding and cooperation. We welcome our partners from civil society organizations and all our guests for today's discussions. At this juncture, may I request the Committee Secretary to acknowledge the resource persons present for today.

asr-000070
00:32:48.740 --> 00:33:03.020
Committee Secretary: Thank you, Mr. Chair. Good afternoon. Good afternoon also to Senator Lacson. For the consultation with civil society organizations to discuss budgetary priorities for the FY 2027 General Appropriations Act or GAA, we would like to acknowledge our resource persons.

asr-000071
00:33:03.020 --> 00:33:37.560
Committee Secretary: First, from the People's Budget Coalition, we have Mr. Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante together with Ms. Zy-za Nadine Suzara, Mr. Adolfo Jose Montesa and Ms. Maxine Valdez. For GoodGovPH, we have Mr. Michel Andre Macahilo. From Social Watch Philippines, we have Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza, who is also a professor of UP NCPAG, together with Mr. Alci Kitalig and Ms. Desiree Peña-Flor. From the Caucus of Development NGO Networks or CODE-NGO, we have Ms. Catherine Basalote together with Ms. Samantha May Santos and Mr. Lawrence Kenneth Castillo.

asr-000072
00:33:38.020 --> 00:34:06.260
Committee Secretary: From Citizen Watch Philippines, we have Ms. Julia Christine Baza. From Democracy Watch Philippines, we have Mr. Lloyd Ian Zaragoza. From FOI Youth Initiative or FYI, we have Mr. Aljon Patrick Acupan. From Action for Economic Reforms, we have Atty. Paula Mae Tanquieng together with Ms. Roshek Sims and Ms. Emily Joy Capule. From the Samahan ng Nagkakaisang Pamilya ng Pantawid or SNPP, we have Ms. Annabelle Luna together with Ms. Jeana Catacio.

asr-000073
00:34:06.700 --> 00:34:39.900
Committee Secretary: From World Vision Philippines, we have Ms. Pauline Navarro. From Unang Hakbang Foundation, Inc., we have Ms. Mary Aieen Padoga. From E-Net Philippines, we have Prof. Flora Arellano together with Ms. Mercy Mitsichan. From the Center for Youth Advocacy and Networking or CYAN or Multiply-Ed, we have Mr. Humphrey Soriano together with Ms. Isaiah Sosa and Ms. Krista Nicole Buat. From the Ateneo Center for Research and Innovation or ACRI, we have Dr. Geminn Louis Apostol together with Dr. Theo Prudencio Juhani Capeding.

asr-000074
00:34:40.240 --> 00:35:15.880
Committee Secretary: From the Medical Action Group or MAG and UHC Collective, we have Dr. Juan Antonio Perez III, who is also the former Undersecretary for Population Development Integration of the CPD. From the Healthcare Professionals Alliance Against COVID-19 or HPAAC, we have Dr. Alberto Ong Jr. From the Philippine Alliance of Patient Organizations or PAPO, we have Ms. Arsenia Torres. From the Youth for Health Coalition, we have Ms. Aliyah May Lozari and Ms. Arriane dela Cruz. From the Youth for Mental Health Coalition or Y4MH, we have Ms. Ray Alyannah Ysabel Lagasca.

asr-000075
00:35:15.880 --> 00:35:44.660
Committee Secretary: From the Filipino Sign Language National Network or FSLN2, we have Dr. Liza Martinez. From the Philippine Anti-Discrimination Alliance of Youth Leaders or PANTAY, we have Mr. Aaron James Villapando. From Aksyon Klima Pilipinas or AKP, we have Mr. John Leo Algo and Ms. Martha Balagal. From Magsasaka at Siyentipiko para sa Pag-unlad ng Agrikultura or MASIPAG, we have Ms. Ira Angela Domingo and Mr. John Althani Famador.

asr-000076
00:35:44.660 --> 00:36:11.760
Committee Secretary: That's it, Mr. Chair. I'm sorry. We also have representatives from the Move As One Coalition: Mr. Luisito Hepuela and Dr. Maureen Ava Mata. From Renacimiento Manila, Ms. Bea Dolores together with Mr. Crisostomo Miguel Ordonez III and Mr. Matthew Gabriel Caudal. And last but not the least, from the Public Services Labor Independent Confederation or PSLink, Dr. Annie Enriquez-Geron. Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000077
00:36:12.440 --> 00:36:35.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Comsec. Magandang araw po sa ating lahat, lalo na sa ating mga kasamahan sa Senado at sa ating mga katuwang mula sa civil society organizations. Every peso we allocate represents a choice about the kind of future we want for our people. These choices must be informed by the experiences of the communities we serve. This is why your participation in the budget process matters.

asr-000078
00:36:35.940 --> 00:37:01.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Noong nakaraang taon, nagsagawa ng konsultasyon sa mga civil society organizations ang ating Senate President Sherwin Gatchalian, na noon ay chairperson ng Committee on Finance. We recognize the foundation he laid for greater public participation in our budget deliberations. Under our chairmanship, we kept building on that effort by bringing your participation directly into the budget hearings.

asr-000079
00:37:02.220 --> 00:37:26.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sinulatan natin ang mga vice chairperson ng Committee on Finance upang mabigyan ng puwang ang mga CSO sa mga pagdinig ng kanilang mga subcommittee. May ilang vice chairperson natin na nag-imbita ng mga CSO at iba pang grupo upang makaupo sa mga hearing at maibahagi ang kanilang mga pananaw sa mga panukalang budget ng mga ahensya.

asr-000080
00:37:27.120 --> 00:37:55.500
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We also invited you to submit questions that we could raise on your behalf. Sinama natin ang inyong mga tanong at alalahanin sa pagbusisi ng budget ng bawat ahensya. Ipinadala rin natin ang mga ito sa mga kinauukulang departamento upang mabigyan ng kaukulang pansin, sagot at aksyon. We want your participation to have a meaningful place in the scrutiny of the proposed budgets of our national government

asr-000081
00:37:55.500 --> 00:38:21.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: agencies, in the questions officials are asked to answer and in the priorities we put forward. Mahalaga ang inyong ambag dahil marami sa inyo ang direktang nakikipag-ugnayan sa mga komunidad. Your experience helps us to achieve our goal of going back to basics. As we prepare our 2027 budget, you help us assess whether the proposed allocations respond to the actual needs of the people.

asr-000082
00:38:22.180 --> 00:38:57.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Today, we are also working to make budget information more accessible and useful to the public. Kasalukuyan nating isinusulong ang pagsasama sa Senate Budget Transparency Portal ng ilan sa mga tools ng ating mga katuwang, kabilang ang People's Budget Coalition at Better Gov PH. Through this effort, we hope to bring these tools to a wider audience and help more Filipinos understand, examine and monitor the national budget. Transparency is more felt when people can actually use the information to ask questions and hold their government accountable.

asr-000083
00:38:58.280 --> 00:39:21.760
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: We're applying the same commitment to transparency in our scrutiny of the proposed DPWH budget na tumaas ng higit P11.49 billion sa ilalim ng General Appropriations Bill. Mula sa 11,420 projects under the 2027 NEP, lumaki rin po ang kabuuang bilang ng mga proyekto sa 16,244 sa ilalim ng GAB.

asr-000084
00:39:22.780 --> 00:39:58.300
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kapansin-pansin din po sa aming pagsusuri ang paglobo ng pondo sa ilalim ng DPWH Convergence Program tulad ng mga multipurpose buildings at basic infrastructure projects na umabot sa P74 billion. Samantala, binawasan ng higit P73 billion ang pondo para sa malalaking foreign-assisted projects na importante sa pagpapalago ng ating ekonomiya. Ito rin ang dahilan kung kaya bumuo tayo ng isang dedicated na team na nakatutok lamang sa masusing line-by-line review ng NEP at General Appropriations Bill mula sa Kamara.

asr-000085
00:39:58.300 --> 00:40:24.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Sinuri po natin ang mga pagbabago sa nakalaang pondo at bilang ng mga proyekto, ang kanilang mga supporting documents at kung may repetition o pag-uulit sa mga proyektong may nakalaang pondo sa kasalukuyang budget. Our initial review has flagged about P266 billion worth of projects for further scrutiny and review, including concerns over the supporting documents submitted to the Committee.

asr-000086
00:40:25.720 --> 00:40:52.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Of the 16,244 total projects under the DPWH operations budget, only 1,418 projects, or 8.73%, were submitted with accompanying physical or digital documentation. A staggering 14,826 projects, or 91.27%, had no submitted supporting documents.

asr-000087
00:40:52.980 --> 00:41:24.900
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Kasama rin po dito ang 23 line items na may laang pondo sa ilalim ng 2026 General Appropriations Act na may kabuuang halaga ng P227.2 million. We also note several lump-sum line items worth P20.5 billion under the GAB. These findings require clear explanations from the DPWH at mahalaga na bago tayo maglaan ng pondo, malinaw ang batayan, pangangailangan at dokumentasyon ng bawat proyekto.

asr-000088
00:41:25.860 --> 00:41:59.400
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Beyond this year's budget review, we want these reforms to endure beyond one's chairmanship, Senate Committee on Finance or budget cycle. Kaya po ngayong araw, bago ang pagbubukas ng konsultasyon na ito kasama ang civil society organizations at government watchdogs, naghahain tayo ng tatlong panukalang batas upang mapagtibay at gawing mas makabuluhan ang pakikilahok ng ating mga mamamayan sa pagbabalangkas, pamamahala at paglalaan ng pondo ng bayan.

asr-000089
00:41:59.880 --> 00:42:29.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: First, the Bantay Budget Act or Senate Bill No. 2576, which seeks to institutionalize CSO participation in the preparation and authorization of the budget. It provides avenues for you to submit proposals, participate in budget hearings and access budget documents, including records of bicameral conference proceedings. Second, the Grassroots Participatory Budgeting Act or Senate Bill No. 2577 seeks

asr-000090
00:42:29.780 --> 00:42:34.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: to bring community-identified priorities into local and national budgeting.

asr-000091
00:42:35.020 --> 00:42:40.220
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Layunin natin magsimula sa mga komunidad ang pagtukoy sa mga proyektong kailangan nila

asr-000092
