00:58:38.740 --> 00:58:40.280
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: that AJ Montesa be recognized po?

asr-000529
00:58:40.960 --> 00:58:42.460
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Yes, TJ Montesa.

asr-000530
00:58:43.260 --> 00:58:44.160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: You're recognized.

asr-000531
00:58:47.220 --> 00:58:48.620
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Yes, magandang hapon po,

asr-000532
00:58:48.760 --> 00:58:50.980
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Chair JV, SP Win, and Senator Ping.

asr-000533
00:58:51.580 --> 00:58:52.700
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Ako po si AJ Montesa

asr-000534
00:58:52.700 --> 00:58:54.060
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: from the People's Budget Coalition.

asr-000535
00:58:54.700 --> 00:58:56.740
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Lampas isang trilyon pesos po

asr-000536
00:58:56.740 --> 00:58:58.280
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: ang red flags na nakita namin

asr-000537
00:58:58.280 --> 00:58:59.560
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: sa 2027 budget.

asr-000538
00:59:00.160 --> 00:59:02.580
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: 210 billion pesos sa soft pork

asr-000539
00:59:02.580 --> 00:59:04.540
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: sa anyon ng patronage-driven

asr-000540
00:59:04.540 --> 00:59:07.040
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: ayuda. 695 billion

asr-000541
00:59:07.040 --> 00:59:08.400
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: sa hard pork, which are

asr-000542
00:59:08.400 --> 00:59:09.780
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: politicized infrastructure.

asr-000543
00:59:10.400 --> 00:59:12.320
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: And 112 billion pesos po sa

asr-000544
00:59:12.320 --> 00:59:14.720
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: shadow pork, o yung unprogrammed appropriations.

asr-000545
00:59:15.460 --> 00:59:16.020
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: In our assessment,

asr-000546
00:59:16.440 --> 00:59:18.540
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: altogether, these produce a budget that serves

asr-000547
00:59:18.540 --> 00:59:20.780
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: politicians before it serves the people.

asr-000548
00:59:21.680 --> 00:59:23.040
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: BBC's National Coordinator,

asr-000549
00:59:23.040 --> 00:59:24.680
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Abigail Absmodalis, should,

asr-000550
00:59:24.700 --> 00:59:26.540
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: be the one speaking here in my place today.

asr-000551
00:59:27.160 --> 00:59:28.920
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: But Abs's mother was recently diagnosed

asr-000552
00:59:28.920 --> 00:59:30.740
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: with cancer. And when she

asr-000553
00:59:30.740 --> 00:59:32.600
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: brought her mother home from the emergency room

asr-000554
00:59:32.600 --> 00:59:34.900
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: last October 11 with a 77,000

asr-000555
00:59:34.900 --> 00:59:36.520
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: peso bill for chemotherapy

asr-000556
00:59:36.520 --> 00:59:38.580
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: complications, PhilHealth

asr-000557
00:59:38.580 --> 00:59:40.180
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: covered only 11,000 pesos.

asr-000558
00:59:40.820 --> 00:59:42.600
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: So she did what thousands of

asr-000559
00:59:42.600 --> 00:59:43.860
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Filipinos do every day.

asr-000560
00:59:44.500 --> 00:59:45.980
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: She wrote to politicians' offices

asr-000561
00:59:45.980 --> 00:59:48.200
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: asking for a guarantee letter

asr-000562
00:59:48.200 --> 00:59:49.820
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: but came away with nothing.

asr-000563
00:59:50.780 --> 00:59:52.780
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: This is the system that the House of Representatives

asr-000564
00:59:52.780 --> 00:59:53.820
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: chooses to feed.

asr-000565
00:59:54.700 --> 00:59:56.900
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Public money for medical and crisis assistance

asr-000566
00:59:56.900 --> 00:59:59.200
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: that reaches the people if the right

asr-000567
00:59:59.200 --> 01:00:00.010
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: politician and the right people

asr-000568
01:00:00.010 --> 01:00:06.360
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: The National Expenditure Program proposed an amount of P72 billion for these ayuda lines.

asr-000569
01:00:06.980 --> 01:00:14.260
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: AICS, MAIFIP, TUPAD, Presidential Assistance for Farmers and Fisherfolk, Tulong Dunong, worth P72 billion.

asr-000570
01:00:15.160 --> 01:00:21.060
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: The House of Representatives gives this P137 billion, nearly double for ayuda.

asr-000571
01:00:21.320 --> 01:00:29.680
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Year after year, the House tends to bloat these programs that give preferential treatment to beneficiaries through letters that legislators hold,

asr-000572
01:00:30.200 --> 01:00:37.460
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: lodged in the budgets of DSWD, DOH, and DOLE, which implicitly carve out these funds for the individual legislators.

asr-000573
01:00:38.880 --> 01:00:46.720
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Bukot pa dito, binawasan pa po ng Kamara ang health promotion, immunization, and health facilities upang madagdagan ang budget ng MAIFIP.

asr-000574
01:00:46.960 --> 01:00:52.340
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: So it seems that the House wants us to get more sick so that we can beg more for our hospital bills.

asr-000575
01:00:53.120 --> 01:00:58.300
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: So based on this, we respectfully ask that the Senate help us advance four reforms to address soft pork.

asr-000576
01:00:58.900 --> 01:00:59.720
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Una, ilipan.

asr-000577
01:01:00.000 --> 01:01:03.820
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Bukot po ang pondo mula sa pabor, mula patungo sa karapatan.

asr-000578
01:01:04.240 --> 01:01:07.260
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Realign the House's ayuda increases to the rules-based programs.

asr-000579
01:01:07.680 --> 01:01:14.680
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: For example, from MAIFIP to PhilHealth, from Tulong Dunong to Tertiary Education Subsidy, and from AICS to 4Ps.

asr-000580
01:01:15.600 --> 01:01:22.100
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Pangalawa po, tanggalin ang guarantee letter at referral letter system, pati ang mga nakatagong alokasyon para sa mga politiko.

asr-000581
01:01:22.280 --> 01:01:26.380
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: So write into the special provisions of AICS, MAIFIP, TUPAD, and PAFF

asr-000582
01:01:26.380 --> 01:01:30.320
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: that referrals and guarantee letters come only from the implementing agency

asr-000584
01:01:30.360 --> 01:01:34.380
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Or hospital social services, never from legislators and their staff.

asr-000585
01:01:34.880 --> 01:01:39.420
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: And to ban allocations reserved for individual legislators with penalties for violations.

asr-000586
01:01:40.920 --> 01:01:49.880
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Pangatlo po, set clear processing timelines, priority lanes for medical and funeral emergencies, alternatives for people without complete documents or PhilSys ID,

asr-000587
01:01:50.240 --> 01:01:54.920
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: and a public appeals process so people know where to apply and how long they'll wait and to contest a denial.

asr-000588
01:01:54.920 --> 01:01:59.860
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: At pang-apat, panatilihing bukas ang pinto gaya ng ginagawa natin po ngayon.

asr-000589
01:02:00.360 --> 01:02:05.000
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Make CSO participation a regular, written part of the Senate's budget process

asr-000590
01:02:05.000 --> 01:02:09.700
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: because we are the ones who live with the effects of every decision in the national budget.

asr-000591
01:02:10.080 --> 01:02:14.400
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Adolfo Jose Montesa: Salamat po, Mr. Chair. I'll turn it over po to my colleague, Ms. Ziza Suzara, with your permission.

asr-000592
01:02:14.580 --> 01:02:15.140
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, AJ.

asr-000593
01:02:16.020 --> 01:02:16.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Tiga, please.

asr-000594
01:02:24.920 --> 01:02:26.540
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Good afternoon, Mr. Ziza.

asr-000595
01:02:26.800 --> 01:02:27.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ziza.

asr-000596
01:02:27.400 --> 01:02:28.800
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Yes. Good afternoon, Ms. Ziza.

asr-000613
01:02:29.480 --> 01:03:03.500
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Senate President Win Gatchalian and Senator Ping Lacson. We in the People's Budget Coalition welcome the landmark ruling of the Supreme Court on the unprogrammed appropriations. But we cannot move forward without accountability. The use of the unprogrammed appropriations has been shrouded in opacity since 2022. Based on our analysis, P499 billion was certified by the Treasury as available for the UA in 2024 to 2025 alone.

asr-000625
01:03:03.700 --> 01:03:11.720
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Half a trillion pesos, controversially drawn from PhilHealth, PDIC, and other GOCC funds

asr-000626
01:03:11.720 --> 01:03:18.860
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: as authorized under the now unconstitutional special provision 1D of the 2024 UA.

asr-000627
01:03:19.500 --> 01:03:25.180
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Hindi pa kasama ang mga ginamit na pondo sa 2022 at 2023.

asr-000628
01:03:25.620 --> 01:03:28.600
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Out of the 499 billion,

asr-000629
01:03:29.460 --> 01:03:33.900
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: 393 billion in total was released to different agencies.

asr-000630
01:03:34.940 --> 01:03:39.120
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: No one knows how these funds were actually expended.

asr-000631
01:03:39.820 --> 01:03:48.180
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: 40% or 195 billion of the 493 billion was released to DPWH.

asr-000632
01:03:49.440 --> 01:03:53.020
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: 107 billion of that went to flood control.

asr-000633
01:03:53.540 --> 01:03:55.520
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Pagkatapos ng flood control scan,

asr-000634
01:03:55.620 --> 01:03:59.440
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: papatanong ka, may substandard at ghost projects rin?

asr-000635
01:03:59.460 --> 01:04:00.640
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Kaya sa mga ito?

asr-000636
01:04:01.180 --> 01:04:06.160
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Furthermore, 29 billion was released to DSWD for AICS.

asr-000637
01:04:06.540 --> 01:04:09.800
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: 10 billion was released to DOH for MAEFIP.

asr-000638
01:04:10.260 --> 01:04:13.620
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Tulad ng LGS, lalong-lalo na ang Falgo.

asr-000639
01:04:14.160 --> 01:04:20.720
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Extra hard pork at soft pork rin pala ang naging priority sa unprogrammed appropriations.

asr-000640
01:04:21.280 --> 01:04:27.280
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: The bloating of the UA and the cuts in the FAPs over the past fiscal years

asr-000641
01:04:27.280 --> 01:04:29.280
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: are two sides of the...

asr-000642
01:04:29.460 --> 01:04:30.300
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: of the same coin.

asr-000643
01:04:30.780 --> 01:04:34.920
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: As the UA became a dumping ground for deprioritized FAPs.

asr-000644
01:04:35.420 --> 01:04:39.140
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Compared to the insertions that replaced them in the HGAB,

asr-000645
01:04:39.600 --> 01:04:44.180
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: FAPs undergo a lengthy process of technical scrutiny and approval.

asr-000646
01:04:44.180 --> 01:04:47.180
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: They must remain in the programmed appropriations.

asr-000647
01:04:48.600 --> 01:04:49.320
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Mr. Chair,

asr-000648
01:04:49.740 --> 01:04:50.480
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Senate President,

asr-000649
01:04:50.760 --> 01:04:51.640
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Senator Lacson,

asr-000650
01:04:51.840 --> 01:04:58.280
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: isa lang ang pinupuntahan ng mga analysis ng PBC sa UA, FAPs at LGSF.

asr-000651
01:04:58.820 --> 01:04:59.180
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: The National...

asr-000652
01:04:59.460 --> 01:05:04.180
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: The national budget is undeniably captured by patronage politics.

asr-000653
01:05:04.620 --> 01:05:12.100
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: So much so that the fiscal program gets extremely distorted every single year since 2022.

asr-000654
01:05:12.900 --> 01:05:20.080
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: This corrosive budget politics has eroded overall budget credibility and public trust.

asr-000655
01:05:20.500 --> 01:05:27.460
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: It is us, taxpayers, who bear the consequences of these fiscally irresponsible choices.

asr-000656
01:05:27.460 --> 01:05:29.140
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: This should end.

asr-000657
01:05:29.460 --> 01:05:36.420
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: We call on the Senate to recast the 2027 budget into a genuinely people-centered budget.

asr-000658
01:05:36.420 --> 01:05:45.420
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: And we urge the Senate as well to conduct a full inquiry on the use of the 2022 to the 2025 unprogrammed appropriations.

asr-000659
01:05:46.660 --> 01:05:47.720
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: Thank you, Mr. Chair.

asr-000660
01:05:47.920 --> 01:05:50.360
People's Budget Coalition Representative Zy-za Nadine Suzara: I turn it over to Ken Abante.

asr-000661
01:05:51.060 --> 01:05:51.980
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you, Ziza.

asr-000662
01:05:53.160 --> 01:05:53.720
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Ken?

asr-000663
01:05:57.720 --> 01:05:59.060
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Maraming salamat po, Chair.

asr-000664
01:05:59.060 --> 01:06:05.380
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Finally, we would like to flag billions of pesos in hard pork or infrastructure program.

asr-000665
01:06:05.920 --> 01:06:08.720
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Sabi nga po namin sa mga nakaraang hearing,

asr-000666
01:06:09.240 --> 01:06:15.200
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: ang warning po namin sa publiko ay posibleng magkaroon ulit tayo ng flood control scandal sa ibang ahensya

asr-000667
01:06:15.200 --> 01:06:18.000
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: if we allow the House budget to pass as is.

asr-000668
01:06:18.480 --> 01:06:23.920
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: This is the same modus operandi of the insertions of Speaker Martin Romualdes and Congressman Zaldico

asr-000669
01:06:23.920 --> 01:06:25.940
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: na nagdala po sa atin sa sitwasyong ito.

asr-000670
01:06:25.940 --> 01:06:28.940
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Nag-insert ng proyektong walang batayang dokumento.

asr-000671
01:06:29.780 --> 01:06:37.660
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Heto po ang updated partial and unofficial results ng aming risk analysis of infrastructure budgets as of October 26, 2026.

asr-000672
01:06:38.420 --> 01:06:46.560
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Halos 7,000 projects worth 190 billion pesos ang in-insert ng House na walang published project attachments.

asr-000673
01:06:47.280 --> 01:06:52.800
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: In the DPWH, the House inserted nearly 6,200 projects worth 172 billion.

asr-000674
01:06:53.420 --> 01:06:55.240
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Many of them are multi-purpose buildings.

asr-000675
01:06:55.940 --> 01:06:58.940
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: In the DOH, the House inserted more than 180 projects.

asr-000676
01:06:59.780 --> 01:07:05.120
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: New health facilities worth more than 2 billion pesos, but they cut the overall health facilities budget.

asr-000677
01:07:05.940 --> 01:07:13.380
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: In the Department of Agriculture, the House inserted more than 350 new farm-to-market roads worth nearly 6 billion pesos,

asr-000678
01:07:13.880 --> 01:07:23.260
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: with some coordinates in the Benham Rise, in Celebesi, and some buildings are even in Algeria and Nigeria.

asr-000679
01:07:23.260 --> 01:07:28.900
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: In the National Irrigation Administration, the House inserted more than 200 new irrigation projects,

asr-000680
01:07:29.060 --> 01:07:32.940
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: worth more than 7 billion pesos, with some cost assumptions that are questionable.

asr-000681
01:07:33.320 --> 01:07:42.140
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: We note, Mr. Chair, that this does not yet include the master list of allocations from the Department of Education schools to check

asr-000682
01:07:42.140 --> 01:07:49.040
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: so that ordinary citizens and media can check whether the places with the highest shortages are really the ones getting the funds.

asr-000683
01:07:50.060 --> 01:07:52.560
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Hindi po namin sinasabi na katiwalian ang lahat ng ito.

asr-000684
01:07:52.900 --> 01:07:55.100
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Kailangan po natin ng infrastrukturang ito.

asr-000685
01:07:55.420 --> 01:07:56.580
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Pero sana maayos.

asr-000686
01:07:56.580 --> 01:07:58.500
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: At ang panawagan po namin,

asr-000687
01:07:59.060 --> 01:08:00.740
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: kung walang published na dokumento,

asr-000688
01:08:01.280 --> 01:08:02.440
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: tanggalin ng Senado.

asr-000689
01:08:03.200 --> 01:08:04.520
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: I-vito ng Pangulo.

asr-000690
01:08:05.160 --> 01:08:08.080
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Sa budget na pinaghirapang buwis ng taong bayan,

asr-000691
01:08:08.540 --> 01:08:09.740
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: bawal magkatay po.

asr-000692
01:08:10.600 --> 01:08:11.600
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Ang worry po namin,

asr-000693
01:08:11.780 --> 01:08:16.560
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: hindi pa rin po natututo o nahiya ang kamera sa kabila ng lahat ng pagmamarcha at rally namin.

asr-000694
01:08:17.120 --> 01:08:18.780
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Sa kabila ng sigaw ng taong bayan,

asr-000695
01:08:18.920 --> 01:08:20.000
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: hindi pa rin natauhan.

asr-000696
01:08:20.640 --> 01:08:25.380
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: But we are thankful that our honorable senators are listening to our calls for systemic reforms.

asr-000697
01:08:25.380 --> 01:08:28.840
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Night and day po talaga yung pakiramdam naming budget advocates.

asr-000698
01:08:29.060 --> 01:08:37.040
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Kaya po ngayon, inilulunsad namin ang Budget Insertions Tracker sa budget.bettergov.ph

asr-000699
01:08:37.040 --> 01:08:42.280
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: so that every taxpayer, every voter, every Filipino can be empowered to demand

asr-000700
01:08:42.280 --> 01:08:45.260
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: that their legislators explain insertions in their districts.

asr-000701
01:08:45.820 --> 01:08:49.180
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Dito po nakasaad ang top districts with the biggest allocations,

asr-000702
01:08:49.580 --> 01:08:52.380
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: with the biggest insertions, even with the biggest cuts.

asr-000703
01:08:52.380 --> 01:08:58.740
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: You can click on every district and see all the 18,000 projects,

asr-000705
01:08:59.040 --> 01:09:03.680
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Including the 7,000 projects that they inserted.

asr-000706
01:09:04.220 --> 01:09:06.400
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: We incorporated these over the weekend.

asr-000707
01:09:06.820 --> 01:09:10.780
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: At ang nakita po namin na may pinakamalalaking budget in the projects that the House added,

asr-000708
01:09:11.400 --> 01:09:15.260
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Ilocos Norte, 1st District, 4.375 billion.

asr-000709
01:09:15.720 --> 01:09:18.620
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Misamis Occidental, 2nd District, 1.8 billion.

asr-000710
01:09:19.160 --> 01:09:21.700
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Davao de Oro, 2nd District, 1.7 billion.

asr-000711
01:09:22.200 --> 01:09:25.180
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Isabela, 4th District Office, 1.7 billion.

asr-000712
01:09:25.840 --> 01:09:28.820
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: South Cotabato, 2nd District Office, 1.6 billion.

asr-000713
01:09:29.040 --> 01:09:31.640
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Bohol, 1st District, 1.5 billion.

asr-000714
01:09:32.180 --> 01:09:35.080
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Nueva Ecija, 1st District, 1.3 billion.

asr-000715
01:09:35.400 --> 01:09:37.560
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Patanga, 2nd District, 1.3 billion.

asr-000716
01:09:37.940 --> 01:09:41.060
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Zambale, 2nd District, 1.2 billion pesos.

asr-000717
01:09:41.220 --> 01:09:43.940
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Ito po ang mga district engineering offices.

asr-000718
01:09:44.680 --> 01:09:47.580
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: We need to reimagine our people power in the budget.

asr-000719
01:09:48.020 --> 01:09:50.160
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: To prevent the cancer of corruption from spreading,

asr-000720
01:09:50.500 --> 01:09:52.740
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: we need to strengthen our nation's immune system.

asr-000721
01:09:52.880 --> 01:09:57.400
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: That means all of us, media, civil society, academe, and oversight agencies

asr-000722
01:09:57.400 --> 01:09:58.840
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: have the data to demonstrate the power of the budget.

asr-000723
01:09:58.840 --> 01:10:03.900
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: To demand accountability from the people who decide on our taxpayer money.

asr-000724
01:10:04.600 --> 01:10:09.020
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Muli po, buwis natin to, boto natin to, at budget natin to.

asr-000725
01:10:09.480 --> 01:10:10.100
People's Budget Coalition Co-convenor Kenneth Isaiah Ibasco Abante: Maraming salamat po.

asr-000726
01:10:11.220 --> 01:10:12.200
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Okay, thank you.

asr-000727
01:10:12.720 --> 01:10:16.360
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Next to present is from GoodGov PH.

asr-000728
01:10:17.520 --> 01:10:20.780
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Presented by Mr. Michel Andre Macahilo.

asr-000729
01:10:21.820 --> 01:10:23.500
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Good afternoon to everyone.

asr-000730
01:10:23.720 --> 01:10:25.420
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: To the Honorable Chair J.V. Ejercito,

asr-000731
01:10:25.580 --> 01:10:27.240
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: to the Senate President, Wyn Gatchalian,

asr-000732
01:10:27.240 --> 01:10:28.240
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: and to the Vice Chairperson,

asr-000733
01:10:28.840 --> 01:10:30.040
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Senator Panfilo Lacson,

asr-000734
01:10:30.400 --> 01:10:31.560
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: we thank the Honorable Committee

asr-000735
01:10:31.560 --> 01:10:33.160
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: in giving us space and the opportunity

asr-000736
01:10:33.160 --> 01:10:35.660
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: to convey our position specific to the youth

asr-000737
01:10:35.660 --> 01:10:37.760
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: in asks with regards to certain programs

asr-000738
01:10:37.760 --> 01:10:39.080
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: in the 2027 budget.

asr-000739
01:10:39.540 --> 01:10:42.500
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: We'd like to zero in on the DepEd Youth Formation Division,

asr-000740
01:10:42.880 --> 01:10:44.780
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: more specifically with their programs

asr-000741
01:10:44.780 --> 01:10:46.280
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: like the Learner Government Program,

asr-000742
01:10:46.640 --> 01:10:48.420
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Career Guidance Program, etc., etc.

asr-000743
01:10:49.060 --> 01:10:49.840
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: What is the problem?

asr-000744
01:10:50.320 --> 01:10:53.100
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Based on our analysis and in the current budget framework,

asr-000745
01:10:53.340 --> 01:10:55.240
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: the LGP and several other programs

asr-000746
01:10:55.240 --> 01:10:56.820
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: such as the Career Guidance Program,

asr-000747
01:10:56.820 --> 01:10:58.820
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: the Learners Formators Enhancement,

asr-000748
01:10:58.840 --> 01:11:00.600
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Enhancement Program, and etc.

asr-000749
01:11:00.600 --> 01:11:02.760
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: remain part of the discretionary funds

asr-000750
01:11:02.760 --> 01:11:04.760
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: of the Bureau of Learner Support Services.

asr-000751
01:11:04.760 --> 01:11:06.760
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Therefore, it remains unclear

asr-000752
01:11:06.760 --> 01:11:09.040
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: whether the program will receive enough funding

asr-000753
01:11:09.040 --> 01:11:11.040
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: to ensure meaningful participation,

asr-000754
01:11:11.040 --> 01:11:14.480
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: capacity building for Supreme Elementary Learner Governments

asr-000755
01:11:14.480 --> 01:11:17.280
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: and likewise Supreme Secondary Learner Governments.

asr-000756
01:11:17.280 --> 01:11:18.240
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Additionally,

asr-000757
01:11:18.240 --> 01:11:21.800
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: P250 million was removed from the budget of the Bureau

asr-000758
01:11:21.800 --> 01:11:23.000
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: when the NEP was passed.

asr-000759
01:11:23.000 --> 01:11:25.440
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: And the second part of the problem is just

asr-000760
01:11:25.440 --> 01:11:28.640
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: public M&amp;E documents specific to the LGP and other

asr-000761
01:11:28.640 --> 01:11:30.520
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: adjacent programs are not recognized.

asr-000762
01:11:30.520 --> 01:11:32.680
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: And we also based on our analysis

asr-000763
01:11:32.680 --> 01:11:36.360
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: that only some regional offices published data about the LGP.

asr-000764
01:11:36.360 --> 01:11:38.640
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: But even then, the published data is either

asr-000765
01:11:38.640 --> 01:11:42.160
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: for certain component programs of the LGP such as elections,

asr-000766
01:11:42.160 --> 01:11:44.440
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: so it's incomplete at the end of the day.

asr-000767
01:11:44.440 --> 01:11:47.160
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Or in existing documents, it's oversimplified

asr-000768
01:11:47.160 --> 01:11:48.480
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: or it comes in passing.

asr-000769
01:11:48.480 --> 01:11:50.720
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Therefore, these programs are heavily insulated

asr-000770
01:11:50.720 --> 01:11:52.280
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: from public scrutiny.

asr-000771
01:11:52.280 --> 01:11:55.160
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Also, recent incidents of school-based violence

asr-000772
01:11:55.160 --> 01:11:58.320
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: across the country highlight the need for avenues for healthy,

asr-000773
01:11:58.320 --> 01:12:01.840
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: socialization, instilling of positive values

asr-000774
01:12:01.840 --> 01:12:04.680
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: and cultivation of love of community and country.

asr-000775
01:12:04.680 --> 01:12:06.160
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: We respectfully ask, therefore,

asr-000776
01:12:06.160 --> 01:12:09.600
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: the Senate Committee on Finance for these specific measures.

asr-000777
01:12:09.600 --> 01:12:13.480
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: First, it's to increase DepEd, BLS, and YFD budget

asr-000778
01:12:13.480 --> 01:12:15.440
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: by at least P250 million.

asr-000779
01:12:15.440 --> 01:12:17.640
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: This is so the Bureau can fund the following.

asr-000780
01:12:17.640 --> 01:12:20.200
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: The institutionalization of after-school programs,

asr-000781
01:12:20.200 --> 01:12:23.600
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: clubs, and organizations so that the DepEd can also do things

asr-000782
01:12:23.600 --> 01:12:25.200
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: like review of the policy framework

asr-000783
01:12:25.200 --> 01:12:28.280
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: on the after-school co-curricular and extracurricular programs.

asr-000784
01:12:28.320 --> 01:12:31.120
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Secondly, it's to strengthen learner governments

asr-000785
01:12:31.120 --> 01:12:33.600
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: as a civic education engagement platform.

asr-000786
01:12:33.600 --> 01:12:35.960
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: That is to say, they will do things like consultations,

asr-000787
01:12:35.960 --> 01:12:38.440
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: policy discussions, and policy validation.

asr-000788
01:12:38.440 --> 01:12:41.280
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Third is to strengthen the career guidance program

asr-000789
01:12:41.280 --> 01:12:44.640
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: and ensure these programs are written as separate line items

asr-000790
01:12:44.640 --> 01:12:49.000
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: to guarantee appropriate funding for these programs

asr-000791
01:12:49.000 --> 01:12:50.840
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: so that they are able to be scrutinized

asr-000792
01:12:50.840 --> 01:12:53.120
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: in cases where budget's insufficient.

asr-000793
01:12:53.120 --> 01:12:56.160
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: To quote EDCOM 2's report on the Filipino learner today,

asr-000794
01:12:56.160 --> 01:12:57.360
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: when adequately...

asr-000795
01:12:58.320 --> 01:12:59.480
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: When adequately supported,

asr-000796
01:12:59.480 --> 01:13:02.120
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: this becomes programs, laboratories rather,

asr-000797
01:13:02.120 --> 01:13:05.320
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: of participation where students deliberate on shared issues,

asr-000798
01:13:05.320 --> 01:13:07.840
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: organize initiatives, and experience responsibility

asr-000799
01:13:07.840 --> 01:13:09.280
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: for collective outcomes.

asr-000800
01:13:09.280 --> 01:13:12.280
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Education for citizenship as articulated in young people

asr-000801
01:13:12.280 --> 01:13:15.120
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: learning to become active citizens is most effective

asr-000802
01:13:15.120 --> 01:13:17.080
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: when it allows the youth to learn, participate,

asr-000803
01:13:17.080 --> 01:13:18.760
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: and reflect and lead within communities

asr-000804
01:13:18.760 --> 01:13:20.080
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: that value their voice.

asr-000805
01:13:20.080 --> 01:13:22.520
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: We therefore urge the Senate to act on these measures

asr-000806
01:13:22.520 --> 01:13:23.720
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: for the Filipino youth,

asr-000807
01:13:23.720 --> 01:13:25.600
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: and to ensure that their learning is holistic

asr-000808
01:13:25.600 --> 01:13:27.120
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: and goes beyond the classroom,

asr-000809
01:13:27.120 --> 01:13:28.160
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: which allows them to have access

asr-000810
01:13:28.160 --> 01:13:30.960
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: to pathways of sustainable outlets and alternatives

asr-000811
01:13:30.960 --> 01:13:32.880
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: compared to the prevailing culture now

asr-000812
01:13:32.880 --> 01:13:34.280
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: where they are nudged to isolation

asr-000813
01:13:34.280 --> 01:13:36.600
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: because of a lack of access to these programs.

asr-000814
01:13:36.600 --> 01:13:39.120
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Learner governments and school-based organizations

asr-000815
01:13:39.120 --> 01:13:40.920
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: offer young people opportunities

asr-000816
01:13:40.920 --> 01:13:42.960
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: to kickstart their respective leadership journeys.

asr-000817
01:13:42.960 --> 01:13:45.920
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Learner governments and clubs can train people in leadership,

asr-000818
01:13:45.920 --> 01:13:48.880
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: civic engagement, and advocacy in their purpose,

asr-000819
01:13:48.880 --> 01:13:51.840
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: which are crucial for leading youth governance institutions

asr-000820
01:13:51.840 --> 01:13:53.800
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: in preparing for public leadership.

asr-000821
01:13:53.800 --> 01:13:56.000
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Again, from GoodGov PH,

asr-000822
01:13:56.000 --> 01:13:58.000
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: maraming salamat at mabuhay ang kabataang Pilipino.

asr-000823
01:13:58.160 --> 01:13:59.160
GoodGovPH Representative Michel Andre D. Macahilo: Thank you.

asr-000824
01:13:59.160 --> 01:14:00.160
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

asr-000825
01:14:00.160 --> 01:14:03.000
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Mr. Michelle Macahilo, next.

asr-000826
01:14:03.000 --> 01:14:06.320
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: On the list is Social Watch Philippines

asr-000827
01:14:06.320 --> 01:14:08.040
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: and NCPAG-UP,

asr-000828
01:14:08.040 --> 01:14:10.800
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza,

asr-000829
01:14:10.800 --> 01:14:14.080
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: co-convenor of Social Watch.

asr-000830
01:14:14.080 --> 01:14:15.640
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: You have the floor.

asr-000831
01:14:15.640 --> 01:14:17.200
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Thank you.

asr-000832
01:14:17.200 --> 01:14:18.640
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Good afternoon.

asr-000833
01:14:18.640 --> 01:14:21.320
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: On behalf of Social Watch Philippines,

asr-000834
01:14:21.320 --> 01:14:23.560
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: I will present our assessment of the proposed

asr-000835
01:14:23.560 --> 01:14:28.000
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: 2027 Budget to the Lens of Social Equity and Human Rights.

asr-000836
01:14:28.160 --> 01:14:32.760
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: My colleagues around the table will subsequently elaborate

asr-000837
01:14:32.760 --> 01:14:34.920
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: on our findings and recommendations.

asr-000838
01:14:34.920 --> 01:14:37.320
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: So, viewed through this lens,

asr-000839
01:14:37.320 --> 01:14:43.320
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: the proposed 2027 budget raises a number of serious concerns.

asr-000840
01:14:43.320 --> 01:14:49.320
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: First, the apparent failure to prioritize the productive sectors,

asr-000841
01:14:49.320 --> 01:14:53.600
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: particularly agriculture, trade, and industry,

asr-000842
01:14:53.600 --> 01:14:57.800
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: which historically has been getting very low public investments,

asr-000843
01:14:58.160 --> 01:14:59.960
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: and it is even lower this year.

asr-000844
01:15:00.000 --> 01:15:07.740
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: These are critical to raising productivity, generating decent employment, and improving people's incomes.

asr-000845
01:15:07.740 --> 01:15:22.340
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: The 2027 proposed budget raises debt service, public works, the defense sector, law and order, while significantly cutting the budget for agriculture, agrarian reform, and trade and industry.

asr-000846
01:15:22.340 --> 01:15:31.740
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: These are the productivity-enhancing sectors, the productivity-enhancing agencies that promote people's incomes, people's livelihoods, and employments.

asr-000847
01:15:32.380 --> 01:15:45.460
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: This tilts the budget towards fiscal obligations, infrastructure, defense, and law and order, and these are prioritized over enhancing productivity and increasing incomes for our people.

asr-000848
01:15:45.940 --> 01:15:47.520
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: This must be addressed.

asr-000849
01:15:47.520 --> 01:15:51.520
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: We are very, very disturbed by the lack of prioritization.

asr-000850
01:15:52.340 --> 01:16:01.800
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: We are very, very disturbed by the lack of prioritization of productivity-enhancing economic activities which our people badly need, particularly in agriculture and MSMEs.

asr-000851
01:16:02.520 --> 01:16:07.020
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Second, so basically this imbalance raises a fundamental question.

asr-000852
01:16:07.020 --> 01:16:20.060
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: How can we aspire to inclusive development without adequately investing in the productive capacities that enable Filipinos to secure decent work and lift themselves outside of poverty?

asr-000853
01:16:20.500 --> 01:16:22.120
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: This is a structural transformation.

asr-000855
01:16:22.920 --> 01:16:25.620
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: If we talk systemic, this is systemic.

asr-000856
01:16:26.880 --> 01:16:31.220
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Second, now we'll talk about human development.

asr-000857
01:16:32.060 --> 01:16:38.960
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: The relegation of people's well-being, dignity, and human development has also been relegated to a secondary concern.

asr-000858
01:16:39.720 --> 01:16:52.320
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Infrastructure and debt service received the highest budgetary increases, while significant budget cuts have yet again been made to health, education, housing, and other essential social needs.

asr-000859
01:16:52.340 --> 01:16:59.480
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Now, this raises budgetary issues about the kinds of priorities of our policymakers.

asr-000860
01:17:00.460 --> 01:17:10.400
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: I'm sorry to say, are we building the foundations for lasting human development, or are we merely managing the consequences of persistent poverty and inequality?

asr-000861
01:17:10.900 --> 01:17:16.720
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: This is very residual social policy rather than transformative.

asr-000862
01:17:16.720 --> 01:17:22.140
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Third, and perhaps most troubling, is the persistence.

asr-000863
01:17:22.340 --> 01:17:32.540
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: This is the result of appropriations vulnerable to pork barrel and patronage politics, which our colleagues in People's Budget Coalition have already very much focused on.

asr-000864
01:17:32.540 --> 01:17:45.560
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Our analysis identifies ₱221 billion of DPWH's BIP program in the House-approved budget, ₱72 billion above the proposed NEP allocation.

asr-000865
01:17:46.340 --> 01:17:52.040
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: These practices are especially troubling in light of the Supreme Court's recent ruling.

asr-000866
01:17:52.040 --> 01:18:06.380
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: This problem of political discretion, now we go to soft pork, extends to social protection programs, which are indispensable in a country marked by widespread poverty and inequality.

asr-000867
01:18:07.220 --> 01:18:16.220
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: The House-approved GAB also contains what may be characterized as soft pork, and our colleagues in PBC have mentioned this in a very thorough way.

asr-000868
01:18:16.220 --> 01:18:21.220
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: At the very least, we urge the Senate to restore their allocations.

asr-000869
01:18:22.040 --> 01:18:28.340
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: to the NEP level, and the freed-up resources go to [unclear]. I will talk about that later in the recommendations.

asr-000870
01:18:28.340 --> 01:18:35.680
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: But let us be clear, the problem is not social protection itself, but its appropriation for political ends.

asr-000871
01:18:37.020 --> 01:18:42.920
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: So consider PhilHealth and MAIFIP, and my colleagues will talk about this much more extensively.

asr-000872
01:18:42.920 --> 01:18:49.920
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: May pakalakang papel naman ang MAIFIP bilang safety net para sa mga pasyenteng kulang ang health coverage.

asr-000874
01:18:50.040 --> 01:18:52.320
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Ngunit meron na tayong PhilHealth eh.

asr-000875
01:18:53.040 --> 01:19:02.060
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Sa ilalim ng Universal Health Care Act, hindi dapat maging permanenteng kapalit ng PhilHealth sa isang parallel system ng medical assistance.

asr-000876
01:19:02.480 --> 01:19:07.040
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Kung kulang ang benepisyon ng PhilHealth sa tamang tugon, ito kasi ng PhilHealth.

asr-000877
01:19:08.000 --> 01:19:10.040
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Hindi patuloy napalakihin ang MAIFIP.

asr-000878
01:19:10.040 --> 01:19:19.440
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Yet in the proposed 2027 budget, PhilHealth remains inadequately funded to fulfill its universal mandate.

asr-000879
01:19:20.040 --> 01:19:26.380
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: While MAIFIP retains substantial allocations, which we all know is vulnerable to patronage politics.

asr-000880
01:19:27.520 --> 01:19:32.780
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Napakasakit ang isang Pilipino, hindi niya dapat itanong, sino ang malalipitan ko?

asr-000881
01:19:33.500 --> 01:19:37.600
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Ang dapat niyang sasabihin, covered ako, karapatan ko to.

asr-000882
01:19:38.400 --> 01:19:46.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Now to LGSF, which stands at 62.62 billion from the HGAB, as we know, is also a kind of pork barrel,

asr-000883
01:19:46.940 --> 01:19:51.120
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: especially the FALBU, the SBDP, and the DRR Assistance Program.

asr-000884
01:19:51.660 --> 01:19:53.520
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: These are all discretionary funds, no?

asr-000885
01:19:54.060 --> 01:19:56.420
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: And are highly vulnerable to patronage politics.

asr-000886
01:19:56.920 --> 01:19:59.720
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: And let's face it, especially as 2028 nears.

asr-000887
01:20:01.100 --> 01:20:08.320
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Adding soft pork, so if we add soft pork that I talked about earlier with the hard pork of BIP and LGSF,

asr-000888
01:20:08.320 --> 01:20:14.640
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: we at least identified about 427 billion in appropriations that warrant rigorous scrutiny

asr-000889
01:20:14.640 --> 01:20:16.760
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: because of their extreme vulnerability.

asr-000890
01:20:16.940 --> 01:20:19.880
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: to political patronage and corruption.

asr-000891
01:20:19.880 --> 01:20:22.740
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: So this brings us to a fundamental question.

asr-000892
01:20:23.240 --> 01:20:26.160
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Whose interest does our national budget ultimately serve?

asr-000893
01:20:26.520 --> 01:20:29.280
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: The Filipino people or those who wield political power?

asr-000894
01:20:30.180 --> 01:20:37.500
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: We cannot ignore the still unresolved flood control corruption scandal involving hundreds of billions of pesos.

asr-000895
01:20:38.160 --> 01:20:41.520
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: It remains an open wound in our national consciousness,

asr-000896
01:20:42.180 --> 01:20:45.440
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: compounded by the continuing absence of meaningful accountability.

asr-000899
01:20:46.940 --> 01:20:49.260
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: The Filipino people have not forgotten.

asr-000900
01:20:50.000 --> 01:20:55.520
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: The recent Supreme Court rulings have reinforced long-standing civil society concerns

asr-000901
01:20:55.520 --> 01:21:03.060
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: over unconstitutional budgetary practices, including unlawful congressional increases in appropriations,

asr-000902
01:21:03.620 --> 01:21:06.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: weakened safeguards over universal appropriations,

asr-000903
01:21:07.400 --> 01:21:12.000
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: prohibited lump-sum appropriations that enable discretionary project allocations,

asr-000904
01:21:12.400 --> 01:21:13.780
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: including for flood control.

asr-000905
01:21:13.780 --> 01:21:16.780
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: As our committee chair,

asr-000906
01:21:16.940 --> 01:21:17.800
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: has said,

asr-000907
01:21:18.160 --> 01:21:21.480
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: these revelations have profoundly eroded public trust,

asr-000908
01:21:21.960 --> 01:21:25.440
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: fueling deep anger and a sense of betrayal.

asr-000909
01:21:26.380 --> 01:21:29.360
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: As such, it is with a sense of urgency that we call on the Senate

asr-000910
01:21:29.360 --> 01:21:32.160
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: to undertake five decisive actions.

asr-000911
01:21:32.640 --> 01:21:38.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: First, scrutinize and remove the estimated 427 billion in appropriations vulnerable to hard and soft pork.

asr-000912
01:21:39.360 --> 01:21:40.640
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Mas malaki yung sa PBC.

asr-000913
01:21:41.740 --> 01:21:43.120
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Dapat isama talaga yan.

asr-000914
01:21:43.120 --> 01:21:45.120
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Second,

asr-000915
01:21:46.940 --> 01:21:48.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: redirect these resources towards agriculture,

asr-000916
01:21:48.940 --> 01:21:50.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: trade and industry

asr-000917
01:21:50.940 --> 01:21:52.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: to raise productivity,

asr-000918
01:21:52.940 --> 01:21:54.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: generate decent work,

asr-000919
01:21:54.940 --> 01:21:56.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: and strengthen sustainable employment and livelihoods.

asr-000920
01:21:56.940 --> 01:21:58.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: The most sustainable pathway out of poverty is decent work.

asr-000922
01:22:00.940 --> 01:22:02.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Let's put decent work up in the agenda.

asr-000924
01:22:04.940 --> 01:22:06.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Third,

asr-000925
01:22:06.940 --> 01:22:08.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: increase investments in education,

asr-000926
01:22:08.940 --> 01:22:10.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: health, housing,

asr-000927
01:22:10.940 --> 01:22:12.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: social protection, child protection,

asr-000928
01:22:12.940 --> 01:22:14.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: persons with disabilities,

asr-000929
01:22:14.940 --> 01:22:16.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: and other socially excluded groups.

asr-000930
01:22:16.940 --> 01:22:18.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: And seriously take into account

asr-000931
01:22:18.940 --> 01:22:20.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Social Watch Philippines-ABI proposal,

asr-000932
01:22:20.940 --> 01:22:22.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: which we have submitted to the committee,

asr-000933
01:22:22.940 --> 01:22:26.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: worth ₱302.125 billion,

asr-000935
01:22:26.940 --> 01:22:28.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: and my colleagues will speak to that as well.

asr-000937
01:22:30.940 --> 01:22:32.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Fourth, ensure that the BICAM committee

asr-000938
01:22:32.940 --> 01:22:34.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: operates within its constitutional authority

asr-000939
01:22:34.940 --> 01:22:36.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: with full transparency and accountability,

asr-000941
01:22:38.940 --> 01:22:40.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: consistent with the recent Supreme Court ruling

asr-000942
01:22:40.940 --> 01:22:42.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: and CSO advocacy.

asr-000943
01:22:42.940 --> 01:22:44.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Finally, support the long-pending

asr-000944
01:22:44.940 --> 01:22:46.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: People's Participation

asr-000945
01:22:46.940 --> 01:22:48.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: in the National Budget Bill,

asr-000946
01:22:48.940 --> 01:22:50.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: to finally institutionalize

asr-000947
01:22:50.940 --> 01:22:52.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: citizens' participation

asr-000948
01:22:52.940 --> 01:22:54.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: and strengthen much-needed public oversight

asr-000949
01:22:54.940 --> 01:22:56.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: of budgetary decisions.

asr-000950
01:22:56.940 --> 01:22:58.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: The ultimate measure

asr-000951
01:22:58.940 --> 01:23:00.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: of a national budget

asr-000952
01:23:00.940 --> 01:23:02.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: is about whose lives it improves

asr-000953
01:23:02.940 --> 01:23:04.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: and whose future it secures.

asr-000954
01:23:04.940 --> 01:23:06.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: For many Filipinos, the admonition

asr-000955
01:23:06.940 --> 01:23:08.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Mahiya naman kayo

asr-000956
01:23:08.940 --> 01:23:10.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: no longer seems adequate.

asr-000957
01:23:10.940 --> 01:23:12.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Instead, it has given way

asr-000958
01:23:12.940 --> 01:23:14.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: to a more damning judgment

asr-000959
01:23:14.940 --> 01:23:16.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: of the government.

asr-000960
01:23:16.940 --> 01:23:18.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: This is the depth of disillusionment,

asr-000961
01:23:18.940 --> 01:23:20.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: public disillusionment,

asr-000962
01:23:20.940 --> 01:23:22.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: that our policymakers must confront,

asr-000963
01:23:22.940 --> 01:23:24.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: and the trust that the Senate

asr-000965
01:23:26.940 --> 01:23:28.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: has both the opportunity

asr-000966
01:23:28.940 --> 01:23:30.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: and responsibility to restore.

asr-000967
01:23:30.940 --> 01:23:32.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: We therefore call

asr-000968
01:23:32.940 --> 01:23:34.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: on this August Chamber,

asr-000969
01:23:34.940 --> 01:23:36.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: please do the right thing.

asr-000970
01:23:36.940 --> 01:23:38.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Stand with the Filipino people.

asr-000971
01:23:38.940 --> 01:23:40.940
Social Watch Philippines Co-convenor Dr. Maria Victoria Raquiza: Maraming salamat po.

asr-000972
01:23:40.940 --> 01:23:42.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Thank you.

asr-000973
01:23:42.940 --> 01:23:44.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Isa Marie Vick Rakisa,

asr-000974
01:23:44.940 --> 01:23:46.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: maraming salamat po.

asr-000975
01:23:46.940 --> 01:23:48.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: As always, you've been

asr-000976
01:23:48.940 --> 01:23:50.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: regular here in a lot of

asr-000977
01:23:50.940 --> 01:23:52.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: our advocacies.

asr-000978
01:23:52.940 --> 01:23:54.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: And thank you very much

asr-000979
01:23:54.940 --> 01:23:56.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: for your observations.

asr-000980
01:23:56.940 --> 01:23:58.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: Next is from Caucus of Development

asr-000981
01:23:58.940 --> 01:24:00.940
Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: NGO Networks

asr-000982
