Senator Joseph Victor "JV" G. Ejercito: As represented by co-convenor, Ms. Julia Christine Baza.

asr-001163
01:30:04.880 --> 01:30:12.400
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: Good afternoon, Honorable Chair Ejército, Senate President Katchilyan, and Vice Chair Senator Lawson.

asr-001164
01:30:12.740 --> 01:30:21.080
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: We thank the Senate Committee on Finance for inviting civil society organizations to consult regarding the proposed 2027 budget.

asr-001165
01:30:21.080 --> 01:30:34.540
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: As Congress continues to deliberate, Citizen Watch calls for greater consumer-centered public spending that prioritizes affordability, accessibility, and effective delivery of essential services.

asr-001166
01:30:35.100 --> 01:30:40.120
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: We recognize the importance of adequate government funding for better public service.

asr-001167
01:30:40.440 --> 01:30:50.480
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: However, we also emphasize that increased budget allocations must translate into tangible, measurable, and meaningful benefits for Filipino consumers.

asr-001168
01:30:51.080 --> 01:31:10.820
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: Public spending must prioritize affordable and reliable electricity, accessible healthcare, safe and efficient public transportation, effective flood protection, improved digital services, and stronger consumer protection from the raging cost of living crisis.

asr-001169
01:31:11.820 --> 01:31:20.800
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: We call on Congress and concerned government agencies to ensure that the proposed 2027 budget is implemented.

asr-001170
01:31:21.080 --> 01:31:29.460
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: With transparency, accountability, efficient resource utilization, and strict monitoring of government projects and programs.

asr-001171
01:31:29.980 --> 01:31:45.540
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: Investments must address the everyday needs of Filipino households, particularly low-income and vulnerable communities, while ensuring that public resources are not wasted through inefficiencies, delays, or questionable expenditures.

asr-001172
01:31:46.200 --> 01:31:52.840
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: On healthcare, we welcome the proposed increase in the Cancer Assistance Fund.

asr-001174
01:31:54.140 --> 01:32:05.940
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: And if approved, we urge the Department of Health to ensure that these additional resources are utilized efficiently and without delay to reach more patients and improve access to comprehensive cancer care.

asr-001175
01:32:06.680 --> 01:32:14.660
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: Citizen Watch Philippines previously worked with Senator J.V. Ejercito as the principal author of the National Integrated Cancer Control Act.

asr-001176
01:32:15.080 --> 01:32:20.660
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: At the same time, we emphasize the need to adequately fund our public education system.

asr-001177
01:32:21.080 --> 01:32:31.220
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: As Education Secretary Angara has pointed out, funding gaps in the proposed 2027 budget could slow implementation of critical programs.

asr-001178
01:32:31.220 --> 01:32:36.740
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: We therefore support efforts to restore and augment the funding for these essential programs.

asr-001179
01:32:37.660 --> 01:32:41.540
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: Every peso of taxpayers' money must serve the public interest.

asr-001180
01:32:42.160 --> 01:32:50.220
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: The true measure of the 2027 national budget should be whether Filipino families experiencing lower household expenses,

asr-001181
01:32:51.080 --> 01:32:59.760
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: better access to essential services, greater protection from financial burdens, and meaningful improvements in their quality of life.

asr-001182
01:33:00.420 --> 01:33:10.200
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: For Citizen Watch Philippines, a truly responsive national budget is one whose benefits are not only reflected in government reports and spending figures,

asr-001183
01:33:10.560 --> 01:33:15.060
CitizenWatch Philippines Co-convenor Julia Kristine Basa: but are genuinely felt by ordinary Filipinos in their homes and in their communities.

asr-001184
01:33:15.540 --> 01:33:15.980
